But what about in Lojban? Can one say CUMKI MUNJE or is it
necessary to use a PE'A somewhere?

x1 is POSSIBLE under conditions x2

y1 is a UNIVERSE/COSMOS [complete and ordered entity] of domain/
sphere y2 defined by rules y3.

MUNJE clearly excludes worlds without y3 --rules-- & worlds without 
definable domain boundaries --y2.

As far as i can tell, there's nothing unlojbanical about CUMKI
MUNJE given that the speaker is expected to have in mind x2, y2 &
y3, or else explicitly denies one or all of them with ZI'Os.

(--And "z2 is CALLED z1 by z3" seems as unproblematical as any
